  "full_text": "free your ass no no no entertain god and your ass will follow no yeah what entertain god and your ass will follow yeah that's it yeah so the king of kings i wonder who god's favorite king was ivan the terrible with god the terrible the bible says god is terrible five thousand so i wonder what uh god decided how loud to make the human voice and that affected okay so let me just tell you something God controls all the parameters like for example being able to get into space but not very far at just the right point in history God controls that shit you might think there's not enough degrees of freedom I don't know but it's fucking true so like uh enough design enough design parameters in order to control that shit Let me just tell you, you might doubt God fucking controlled the human voice and how many people could listen. God controlled that shit, I'm telling you. Caring concern for others. Clothe yourself with humility toward one another, for God is opposed to the proud, but gives grace to the humble. Humility of mind is really an attitude, isn't it? It's a preset mentality that determines ahead of time. Thoughts like, I care about those around me. Why do I always have to be first? I'm going to help someone else win for a change. Today I'm going to curb my fierce competitive tendencies. Instead of always thinking about receiving, let's start looking for ways to give. Instead of holding grudges against those who offend us, we'll be anxious to forgive. Instead of keeping a record of what we've done or who we've helped, we'll take delight in forgetting the deeds and being... virtually unnoticed, our hunger for public recognition will diminish in significance.",
